From: OpenWrt Builder <builder@openwrt.org>
Date: Sat, 28 Dec 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: fix RISCV_FENCE redefinition error

The RISCV_FENCE macro is defined in both barrier.h and fence.h,
causing a redefinition error when compiling kernel modules.

Fix by including fence.h in barrier.h and removing the duplicate
definition.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt Builder <builder@openwrt.org>
---
 arch/riscv/include/asm/barrier.h | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/riscv/include/asm/barrier.h
+++ b/arch/riscv/include/asm/barrier.h
@@ -10,14 +10,15 @@
 #ifndef _ASM_RISCV_BARRIER_H
 #define _ASM_RISCV_BARRIER_H
 
+#include <asm/fence.h>
+
 #ifndef __ASSEMBLY__
 
 #define nop()		__asm__ __volatile__ ("nop")
 #define __nops(n)	".rept	" #n "\nnop\n.endr\n"
 #define nops(n)		__asm__ __volatile__ (__nops(n))
 
-#define RISCV_FENCE(p, s) \
-	__asm__ __volatile__ ("fence " #p "," #s : : : "memory")
+/* RISCV_FENCE is now defined in asm/fence.h */
 
 /* These barriers need to enforce ordering on both devices or memory. */
 #define mb()		RISCV_FENCE(iorw,iorw)
